<%# The step to make the pet your own: a word on why, and a card for each
    building block. A side guide (SideGuide) has no review to be rejected
    by, so it says it another way. %>
<section aria-labelledby="your-own">
  <h2 id="your-own">Make it your own!</h2>
  <% if side_guide %>
    <p>Don't just follow this guide and change nothing. Make the project your own! Experiment, and do something entirely different.</p>
  <% else %>
    <p>your project will be rejected if you just follow this guide and change nothing. Make the project your own! Experiment, and do something entirely different.</p>
  <% end %>
  <p>There are so many things you can do, and this guide is here to show you the ropes so you can do something for yourself.</p>
  <p>If you need ideas or help, ask in <a href="https://hackclub.slack.com/archives/C0ASBTMS82H" target="_blank" rel="noopener">#Playground</a> we’ll be glad to help!</p>
  <%# A card for each building block (BuildingBlock), with its demo GIF, so
      the reader sees what it makes. Each opens the block's page in a new
      tab, so the guide stays open where it was. %>
  <ul class="block-cards" aria-label="building blocks">
    <% BuildingBlock.all.each do |block| %>
      <% width, height = block.gif_size %>
      <li>
        <%= link_to building_block_page_path(block), class: "block-card", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" do %>
          <%= image_tag block.gif_asset, alt: "", width:, height:, loading: "lazy", decoding: "async" %>
          <span class="block-card-title"><%= block.title %> <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="visually-hidden">, opens in a new tab</span></span>
        <% end %>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
</section>
